  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "f5e924fbdfc34119a22f6a64f3813285_36",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "6. Be that as it may."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "88adaee129dd49b5baf0ef1ca68adfc1_37",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Considering the fact that prima facie, no case is made out against the present petitioner, as no motive has been attributed to him, and also the fact that he is not involved in commission of murder, petitioner deserves the concession of reg"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "caeaccc959d045669784a4085209a587_38",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The only role assigned to the petitioner was that he was informed by the main accused Sachin, that he would eliminate Devi Singh-deceased as well as handing over his mobile phone to the petitioner so as to avoid his mobile phone location be"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7d72230241ee4154887cfb30c12281ff_41",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This Court has heard the learned counsel for both the parties concerned, and has gone through the entire case file as also the reply filed by the State."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0a65c0394c1249339242b18f06b3cf72_42",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n9. \"Bail is the Rule and Jail is an Exception\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3e2f94791515463a82602a3128f04a15_43",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This basic principle of criminal jurisprudence was laid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court, way back in 1978, in its landmark judgment titled \"State of Rajasthan V. Balchand alias Baliay\", 1977 AIR 2447, 1978 SCR (1) 535."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0a729234c95a43fd8f7413610167f06e_44",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This principle finds its roots in one of the most distinguished fundamental rights, as enshrined in Article 21 of the Constitution of India."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "98939c7596f0429fa7cbea878028f356_45",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Though the underlying objective behind detention of a person is to ensure easy availability of an accused for trial, without any inconvenience, however, in case the presence of an accused can be secured otherwise, then detention is not comp"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d33ac63daad548b9b05c942b258995e1_46",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n10. The right to a speedy trial is one of the rights of a detained person."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cd3f8f452cd34f39b057dac2eff530a5_47",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, while deciding application for regular bail, the Courts shall also take into consideration the fundamental precept of criminal jurisprudence, which is \"the presumption of innocence\", besides the gravity of offence(s)\ninvolved."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "22aa8fdda01540af978f0dff50dee32f_48",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "11. In \"Nikesh Tarachand Shah V. Union of India\", (2018) 11 SCC 1, the Hon'ble Supreme Court has recorded the following:-\n\"14."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b5d88608505d4e47b9e8ff0cb0b1f1f1_49",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Gurbaksh Singh Sibbia v. State of Punjab, (1980) 2 SCC 565 at 586-588, the purpose of granting bail is set out with great felicity as follows:-\n\"27."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8dc2b9acb68a485798de06c659b96032_50",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is not necessary to refer to decisions which deal with the right to ordinary bail because that right does not 4 of 8"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b021cc6df6dc4a238776aabda6ab7d53_51",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Neutral"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "038506514aa443aba1e3d03b39cfc7c0_52",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Citation No:=2024:PHHC:045154"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "742b1e9f880a4b0cab69736716730a18_53",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "furnish an exact parallel to the right to anticipatory bail."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0142200e360f4af7aaea1ad25baa8116_54",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is, however, interesting that as long back as in 1924 it was held by the High Court of Calcutta in Nagendra v.\nKing-Emperor the object of bail is to secure the attendance of the accused at the trial,\nthat the proper test to be applied in"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ca1eb52350094ee5aca582197dc885ca_55",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In two other cases which,significantly, are the 'Meerut Conspiracy cases' observations are to be found regarding the right to bail which deserve a special mention."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e20476100b04495695b2ed97460fdddb_56",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In K.N. Joglekar v. Emperor [AIR 1931 All 504 : 33 Cri LJ 94] it was observed, while dealing with Section 498 which corresponds to the present Section 439 of the Code, that it conferred upon the Sessions Judge or the High Court wide powers "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e242a4b6dbb146ab829ff060090ff135_57",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It was observed by the court that there was no hard and fast rule and no inflexible principle governing the exercise of the discretion conferred by Section 498 and that the only principle which was established was that the discretion should"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c8800b58ed544a9fa6f63c18e699f946_58",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Emperor v. Hutchinson Aman vs State Of Haryana on 3 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/109362341/\n3 [AIR 1931 All 356, 358 : 32 Cri LJ 1271] it was said that it was very unwise to make an attempt to lay down any part"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fa4624235c8c4a06aa473099b7cbe314_59",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "According to the High Court, the variety of cases that may arise from time to time cannot be safely classified and it is dangerous to make an attempt to classify the cases and to say that in particular classes a bail may be granted but not "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3f322c0149714da8a95d1a94a5eadee2_60",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It was observed that the principle to be deduced from the various sections in the Criminal Procedure Code was that grant of bail is the rule and refusal is the exception."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "93f9edaf57cc4468a59142f8b0bb4229_61",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "An accused person who enjoys freedom is in a much better 5 of 8 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:045154 position to look after his case and to properly defend himself than if he were in custody."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "275ac9c699f54fbfa4a3eb52e36999e7_62",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As a presumably innocent person he is therefore entitled to freedom and every opportunity to look after his own case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "32d23b6c6937403ea61d862a90c71030_63",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "A presumably innocent person must have his freedom to enable him to establish his innocence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "16e1d9b9e3c64a73b860c5cea5ce4562_64",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n28. Coming nearer home, it was observed by Krishna Iyer, J., in Gudikanti Narasimhulu v. Public Prosecutor [(1978) 1 SCC 240 : 1978 SCC (Cri) 115] that: (SCC p. 242, para 1) \"... the issue of bail is one of liberty, justice, public safety "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a979105c7997441d8d881d15e1608b4e_65",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "After all, personal liberty of an accused or convict is fundamental, suffering lawful eclipse only in terms of procedure established by law."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f167c83251f14f59a2c7541c2a93b308_66",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The last four words of Article 21 are the life of that human right.\"\n29."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1c935c975e5946d7889fdf087166c28b_67",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Gurcharan Singh v. State (Delhi Administration) [(1978) 1 SCC 118 : 1978 SCC (Cri) 41] it was observed by Goswami, J., who spoke for the court, that:\n(SCC p. 129, para 29) \"There cannot be an inexorable formula in the matter of granting "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "513a01d717de41be851db7b6b6522ee9_68",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The facts and circumstances of each case will govern the exercise of judicial discretion in granting or cancelling bail.\"\n30."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6ec7d9a0600a436a8a9a54abb8d74003_69",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In AMERICAN JURISPRUDENCE (2d, Volume 8, p. 806, para 39), it is stated:\n\"Where the granting of bail lies within the discretion of the court, the granting or denial is regulated, to a large extent, by the facts and circumstances of each par"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f2e3e746bd344bcca7b4356e1d461bd1_70",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Since the object of the detention or imprisonment of the accused is to secure his appearance and submission to the jurisdiction and the judgment of the court, the primary inquiry is whether a recognizance or bond would effect that end.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0090b550f9a048c58a967dcb2517015a_71",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nIt is thus clear that the question whether to grant bail or not depends for its answer upon a variety of 6 of 8 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:045154 circumstances, the cumulative effect of which must enter into the judicial verdict."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8487b22543a446dcbb097d083cded9a3_72",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Any one single circumstance cannot be treated as of universal validity or as necessarily justifying the grant or refusal of bail.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4b450a15e51b4e3292ae581d2ac8f694_73",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nAman vs State Of Haryana on 3 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/109362341/\n4 12."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a2b9a48b4fbc45efa31e1109f839f1ce_74",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Also, in Siddharam Satlingappa Mhetre v. State of Maharashtra, Criminal Appeal No.2271 of 2010, the Hon'ble Supreme Court has insisted upon striking a perfect balance of sanctity of an individual's liberty as well as the interest of the soc"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "150f4725518d44de949ea3b95a229e40_75",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The relevant extract of the judgment (supra) is reproduced hereinafter:-\n\"3."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5b1c527a123f485782d10b8a535f35ee_76",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The society has a vital interest in grant or refusal of bail because every criminal offence is the offence against the State."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c135f44a7dc8456baea19016b769ebdc_77",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The order granting or refusing bail must reflect perfect balance between the conflicting interests, namely, sanctity of individual liberty and the interest of the society."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d459818324374fb893d50952803b754e_78",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The law of bails dovetails two conflicting interests namely, on the one hand, the requirements of shielding the society from the hazards of those committing crimes and potentiality of repeating the same crime while on bail and on the other "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fa0e1c23c59e494dae51b78b2b803ecb_79",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This Court has examined the instant petition on the touchstone of the hereinabove extracted settled and legal principle(s) of law and is of the considered opinion that the instant petition is amenable for being allowed.\n"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "67231c698997496f8fb0d89422a3d34b_80",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "FINAL ORDER 14."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "514eaf4c7d3e460c8e76b2e25cac4f06_81",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Considering the fact that the instant case is based upon circumstantial evidence, the petitioner has suffered incarceration of 08 months and 28 days as on today, the trial is at initial stage and further the 7 of 8 Neutral Citation No:=2024"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0cb6489ff33545f1bb9dd373af33549e_82",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
